(* Each part of each port takes every attribute of its element and passes it
   on, as HeroUI's React components spread the rest of their props on theirs:
   each part is given [data-testid], [class_], [title], [style], a [ref] and an
   [on_key_down], which must reach the element its selector finds -- the ref
   handed it, the handler called on it -- beside the part's own; and then each
   is drawn by an [as_], and all of it must reach what that draws. An svg takes
   no [title]. An avatar's image, which shows only once it has loaded, is
   checked by the avatar's own test. *)

